    "Q14"
  ],
  "notes": "Two distinct failure modes (corrosion bonding on PCV-0005 causing high lift; spring relaxation on four other valves causing low lift) merge into a common consequence (out-of-band setpoints / inoperability) per rule 5. MSRV Automatic Actuation Logic is described as a non-safety-related defense-in-depth electrical system that remained available/operable throughout normal operation, but is not itself an EIIS-coded backup system per se; omitted as a formal BACKED_UP_BY System node since it is design-context/defense-in-depth explanation rather than a stated operable backup system during an inoperability window (no System node created to avoid over-modeling; captured in chain summary and notes only). Eight previous similar LERs across BFN Units 1, 2, 3 all modeled as stub LER nodes per rule 9, keeed keys exactly as stated in narrative (format 'plant-docket/year-seq-rev')."
}